#: manual/conformance.md:9
msgid "This page is QED's single compliance review table. It describes what the shipped implementation and its tests establish. It does not turn implementation evidence into a Lean refinement theorem. The formal dependency and theorem map lives in [`formal_verification/theory-proof-plan.md`](../../formal_verification/theory-proof-plan.md); the branch promotion policy lives in [`formal_verification/branch_contract.md`](../../formal_verification/branch_contract.md). The machine-readable registry is [`qed_obligations.json`](qed_obligations.json), and the proof-obligation matrix is generated into this page below."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:18
msgid "Document architecture"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:20
msgid "The repository keeps three focused review surfaces:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:22
msgid "[Syntax guide](syntax.md): the shipped theorem-script input grammar."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:23
msgid "[Formal description](formal.md): the normative specification entry point and its embedded PDF preview."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:25
msgid "This page: implementation conformance, proof obligations, evidence limits, and contributor checks."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:28
msgid "Package API, design, tutorial, and user-manual pages explain the shipped surface. They do not create parallel governance, audit, changelog, or proof matrix authorities."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:32
msgid "Package and documentation governance"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:34
msgid "The dependency direction is `kernel -> logic/elab -> parser -> tactics -> prover -> cmd`. Only `kernel` may construct theorem objects. Upper layers may organize checked helpers, parse and elaborate input, transform proof states, replay checked paths, and report diagnostics; they may not add logical authority."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:39
msgid "Each package keeps its production and test alias entry points explicit. Changes to semantic boundaries, gates, scope, replay, parser lowering, or theorem lineage must update implementation, regression tests, and this review table. Documentation uses one canonical page per concern and keeps research notes under `research/`; research notes are evidence records, not shipped contracts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:45
msgid "`alias.mbt` exposes only stable imports needed by production code. `alias_test.mbt` mirrors those imports before adding test-only imports, and explicitly imports its own package symbols with `using @<package> {...}`. Alias headers state their scope and maintenance rules; aliases are not a second public API or an unbounded re-export table. The dependency-free `kernel` has only `alias_test.mbt`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:52
msgid "`research_rewrite` depends only on `kernel` and `logic`, and no shipped package depends on it. `cmd` is executable and cannot be imported. Reverse dependencies require a design review; prefer a neutral data structure or explicit bridge. Parser lowering, tactic execution, orchestration, diagnostic rendering, and corpus data keep separate responsibilities."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:58
msgid "Update code and tests first, then the user manual, affected package pages, this review, repository summaries, and relevant research records. Check that generated `.mbti` changes match the intended public boundary. Maintenance-facing pages declare status, audience, authority, scope, and review date; new research belongs under `research/<topic>/` and declares its unshipped, non-authoritative status."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:65
msgid "Current evidence boundary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance.md:67
msgid "The current Typed HOL results cover the fixed-signature core, history-indexed extension closure, and finite declaration-allocation facts. MoonBit snapshot, scope, and theorem-lineage repairs have deterministic regression evidence. Growing-signature transport, source-level MoonBit refinement, syntactic type-definition erasure, and an independent certificate checker remain open obligations. A passing Lean build or MoonBit test must not be reported as a refinement proof."
msgstr ""

